## Workshop: a deterministic resource and manufacturing world: places, gathering, making and delivering, as op codes
## Import it with an alias of your choice: "ws:" u_se< "Workshop".
## Put libs/Workshop/src on XETAL_PATH ("just path"); the reference is libs/Workshop/docs.
## Names with l: are exported; the others are private to this file.
##
## The world of the experiments on tools and policies (the research's
## "resource-gathering and manufacturing game"): four places (1 forest,
## 2 mine, 3 workshop, 4 store), an agent who carries wood and ore,
## makes devices at the workshop from a recipe and delivers them to the
## store. A state is five Ints, (pos, wood, ore, made, delivered); a
## task is (q, w, r): deliver q devices, each made from w wood and r
## ore. Everything an agent can do is one of nine op codes:
##
##   1 go to the forest   2 gather wood (at the forest)
##   3 go to the mine     4 gather ore (at the mine)
##   5 go to the workshop 6 make a device (at the workshop, w wood, r ore)
##   7 go to the store    8 deliver what was made (at the store)
##   9 look (changes nothing)
##
## An op whose precondition does not hold fails and changes nothing.
## The world is pure: the same state and op always give the same
## result, so whole episodes are reproducible.

### The world

## `s_tart @`: the agent at the store with nothing: (4, 0, 0, 0, 0).
l:s_tart := { @ -> (4, 0, 0, 0, 0) }

## `(q, w, r) s_tep ((pos, wood, ore, made, delivered), op)`: the state
## after op, and 1 if it succeeded or 0 if it failed (the state then
## unchanged).
## >> "ws:" u_se< "Workshop"
## >> (2, 1, 1) ws:s_tep ((1, 0, 0, 0, 0), 2)
## ((1, 1, 0, 0, 0), 1)
## >> (2, 1, 1) ws:s_tep ((1, 0, 0, 0, 0), 4)
## ((1, 0, 0, 0, 0), 0)
l:s_tep := { (q, w, r) ((pos, wood, ore, made, delivered), op) ->
  op = 1 ? ((1, wood, ore, made, delivered), 1)
  (op = 2) & pos = 1 ? ((pos, wood + 1, ore, made, delivered), 1)
  op = 3 ? ((2, wood, ore, made, delivered), 1)
  (op = 4) & pos = 2 ? ((pos, wood, ore + 1, made, delivered), 1)
  op = 5 ? ((3, wood, ore, made, delivered), 1)
  (op = 6) & (pos = 3) & (wood >= w) & ore >= r ? ((pos, wood - w, ore - r, made + 1, delivered), 1)
  op = 7 ? ((4, wood, ore, made, delivered), 1)
  (op = 8) & (pos = 4) & made > 0 ? ((pos, wood, ore, 0, delivered + made), 1)
  op = 9 ? ((pos, wood, ore, made, delivered), 1)
  ((pos, wood, ore, made, delivered), 0)
}

## `(q, w, r) d_one state`: 1 once q devices have been delivered.
## >> "ws:" u_se< "Workshop"
## >> (2, 1, 1) ws:d_one (4, 0, 0, 0, 2)
## 1
l:d_one := { (q, w, r) (pos, wood, ore, made, delivered) -> delivered >= q }

### The expert

## `(q, w, r) e_xpert state`: the op a competent agent does next: make
## the devices still needed one at a time (gather the wood, then the
## ore, then make one), then take them all to the store and deliver;
## 0 when the task is done. The experiments' stand-in for a model's
## choice of action: deterministic, always right, and charged for.
## >> "ws:" u_se< "Workshop"
## >> (1, 1, 1) ws:e_xpert ws:s_tart @
## 1
l:e_xpert := { (q, w, r) (pos, wood, ore, made, delivered) ->
  need := q - delivered + made
  have := (wood >= w) & ore >= r
  (need > 0) & have & pos = 3 ? 6
  (need > 0) & have ? 5
  (need > 0) & (wood < w) & pos = 1 ? 2
  (need > 0) & wood < w ? 1
  (need > 0) & pos = 2 ? 4
  need > 0 ? 3
  (made > 0) & pos = 4 ? 8
  made > 0 ? 7
  0
}

## `n_ame op`: an op code's name, for reports.
## >> "ws:" u_se< "Workshop"
## >> ws:n_ame 6
## make
l:n_ame := { op ->
  op = 1 ? "go-forest"
  op = 2 ? "gather-wood"
  op = 3 ? "go-mine"
  op = 4 ? "gather-ore"
  op = 5 ? "go-workshop"
  op = 6 ? "make"
  op = 7 ? "go-store"
  op = 8 ? "deliver"
  op = 9 ? "look"
  "?"
}
